Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.230 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  three easy reasons to visit miami  the weather  the beach  and of course the food  known for its caribbean and latin  american influences there are some  famous dishes that call this city home  but we are here for a few under the  radar spots that still serve up the  classic heat miami is known for  first up a cuban dish but it might not  be what you'd expect  [Music]  if you tell my grandfather to put cheese  on the fritta he'll tell you that's a  cheeseburger not afrida hi i'm george  lepore i'm the co-founder and managing  partner at cuban guys restaurants  frida guana is our version of the great  american hamburger  to make fritta guana we get ground beef  and we season it with a blend of  ingredients that gives it a smoky  chorizo taste  we shred the potatoes and cook the  frittata in the flat grill and it gives  it a nice crunch it tastes so good that  it needs no other ingredients back in  cuba carts were lined up in the streets  like they do with hot dog carts selling  frittas  miami has known the frida since the  early 50s when cuban exiles started  coming to the miami shores i remember  having a friday right around 12 years  old and it's been my passion ever since  next we found an over-the-top sweet spot  to follow savory  what's better than donuts what's better  than ice cream donuts and ice cream  together  it's a whole bunch of flavors it's  something over the top and and that's  what i love  my name is tony bahu i am the owner of  eonuts we are home of the smash donut  located on northwest 136th avenue in  sunrise florida in the greater miami  area so to make a smash donut it's very  simple we take a glazed doughnut we cut  it in half we put a scoop of ice cream  in it  the magic is we hot press it after it's  done we put some toppings on top  we have cereal toppings we have drizzles  we have sprinkles we have really cool  things the beauty of the smashed donut  is the outside is hot the inside stays  cold so you get texture you get flavor  you get temperature you get it all i  just absolutely love watching people try  smash donut for the first time whether  it's an adult a child a big kid whatever  it is just to see that expression on  their face when they try to smash donut  is super super exciting  at one of miami's longest running west  indian grocers there's one dish you  really shouldn't miss my ancestors went  for the caribbean from india and that's  how routine come about my name is nafisa  ali my store name is b m market  located at  21979 street miami florida i've been in  this location for 29 years roti is a  flat bread you make wraps with it as  well as eat it like a piece of bread too  you make a dough then we cut them into a  small size dough roll it out and fill it  with spooky and you bake it on a flat  pan the most popular filling is the jerk  chicken goat the shrimp also the ackee  and saltfish  has a real nice soft smelly texture when  it's really fresh right off the stove  sometimes flaky  very tasty too but roti takes a lot of  practice you have to have the passion  the love the excitement  when you find a really good kebab spot  you shouldn't keep it to yourself so  here you go you're welcome  this is like a german turkish fusion  since i'm like half german half turkish  the food reflects me  my name is oliver fryen the name of my  restaurant spitfire kebab we're located  in a 405 15th street on washington  avenue in miami beach we're making donut  from scratch kabob is made of fresh  bread we slice the bread up we put the  protein in it we have beef chicken or  falafel we garnish it with some salads  like the red cabbage the white cabbage  cucumbers tomatoes and the onions and we  top it off with some tzatziki sauce this  is an explosion of flavors people they  never tried the food before and they got  impressed i opened up this place in  2015. i grew up with this food over in  germany where i learned all the  authentic recipes since we have a lot of  turkish people over there  donna kebab was born in berlin i'm  bringing the original authentic tastes  to the states  [Music]  and finally we have a woman using her  multicultural heritage to create a new  flavor profile  my mother is spanish and my father's  japanese this dish is a unique product  of that perfect combination hi i'm chie  and i'm the owner of yoko matcha it is  located on 26th street and northwest 2nd  avenue in wynwood miami one of our  signature dishes is the matcha pasta  pastelito is a very popular cuban pastry  we found a way to incorporate matcha  into it so the dough is cut up into  pieces and the filling is placed on top  of the dough the matcha filling is made  with matcha  white chocolate cream cheese and  condensed milk the rest is a secret  once it's fully baked and it's delicious  we take it out we let it cool down and  drizzle more matcha and white chocolate  on top and it's that perfect combination  of sweet and bitter this is the best  matcha ever  [Music]  you

